    ["HumanEval/41", "Write the complete Python function `car_race_collision` for this signature and docstring:\n\n\n\ndef car_race_collision(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    Imagine a road that's a perfectly straight infinitely long line.\n    n cars are driving left to right;  simultaneously, a different set of n cars\n    are driving right to left.   The…", "rwrwrww", [10816, 10109, 2883, 2083, 1916, 6701, 3366], ["", "SyntaxError: unterminated string literal…", "", "EOFError: EOF when reading a line", "", "EOFError: EOF when reading a line", "AssertionError"], ["…every other car in the opposite direction, leading to the solution `n * n`.", "…relationship between the number of cars and their potential collisions.", "…to left is the product of the number of cars in each set. \"\"\" return n * n ```", "…to simulate the movement of each car, making it both simple and optimized."]],
    ["HumanEval/42", "Write the complete Python function `incr_list` for this signature and docstring:\n\n\n\ndef incr_list(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return list with elements incremented by 1.\n    >>> incr_list([1, 2, 3])\n    [2, 3, 4]\n    >>> incr_list([5, 3, 5, 2, 3, 3, 9, 0, 123])\n    [6, 4, 6, 3, 4, 4, 10, 1, 124]\n    \"\"\"", "rrrrrrr", [875, 898, 1118, 1345, 881, 782, 1100], ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["…of elements in the list and is straightforward to read and understand.", "…is also O(n) as a new list of the same length as the input list is created.", "…manner, leveraging Python's list comprehension for clarity and performance.", "…empty lists correctly and works for any list of integers provided as input."]],
