    ["HumanEval/44", "Write the complete Python function `change_base` for this signature and docstring:\n\n\n\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>>…", "rrrrrrr", [7429, 1619, 7405, 3583, 6535, 4272, 5226], ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["…digits.append(str(x % base)) x = x // base return ''.join(reversed(digits)) ```", "…of \\( O(\\log_x \\text{base}) \\), which is optimal for such conversions.", "…iterative division and list manipulation, ensuring clarity and correctness.", "…in the specified base using basic arithmetic operations and list manipulations."]],
