    ["HumanEval/48", "Write the complete Python function `is_palindrome` for this signature and docstring:\n\n\n\ndef is_palindrome(text: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if given string is a palindrome\n    >>> is_palindrome('')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('aba')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('aaaaa')\n    True\n    >>> is_palindrome('zbcd')\n   …", "rrrrrrr", [1069, 1143, 974, 1376, 1069, 624, 1826], ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["…as it processes each character once to reverse the string and again to compare.", "…including empty strings and strings with special characters or mixed case.", "…as they are, including spaces and punctuation if they are part of the input.", "…comparison operations. This solution is both optimal and easy to understand."]],
    ["HumanEval/49", "Write the complete Python function `modp` for this signature and docstring:\n\n\n\ndef modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p (be aware of numerics).\n    >>> modp(3, 5)\n    3\n    >>> modp(1101, 101)\n    2\n    >>> modp(0, 101)\n    1\n    >>> modp(3, 11)\n    8\n    >>> modp(100, 101)\n    1\n    \"\"\"", "rwrrrrr", [3210, 1672, 1470, 2391, 1156, 2858, 1530], ["", "AssertionError", "", "", "", "", ""], ["…pow(2, n, p) ```python def modp(n: int, p: int) -> int: return pow(2, n, p) ```", "…required through exponentiation by squaring, ensuring optimal performance.", "…even for very large values of `n`, making it suitable for practical use.", "…feasible limits, making it suitable for practical use in various applications."]],
    ["HumanEval/50", "Write the complete Python function `decode_shift` for this signature and docstring:\n\n\n\ndef encode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    returns encoded string by shifting every character by 5 in the alphabet.\n    \"\"\"\n    return \"\".join([chr(((ord(ch) + 5 - ord(\"a\")) % 26) + ord(\"a\")) for ch in s])\n\n\ndef decode_shift(s: str):\n   …", "rwwrrrr", [2113, 2803, 5549, 3383, 2340, 2103, 13854], ["", "SyntaxError: closing parenthesis ']' does…", "AssertionError", "", "", "", ""], ["…return ''.join([chr((ord(c) - 5 - ord('a')) % 26 + ord('a')) for c in s]) ```", "…the wrapping around the alphabet and correctly decodes the input string.", "…shift while preserving the structure and integrity of the input string.", "…the shift applied during encoding, thus restoring the original string."]],
    ["HumanEval/51", "Write the complete Python function `remove_vowels` for this signature and docstring:\n\n\n\ndef remove_vowels(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    remove_vowels is a function that takes string and returns string without vowels.\n    >>> remove_vowels('')\n    ''\n    >>> remove_vowels(\"abcdef\\nghijklm\")\n    'bcdf\\nghjklm'\n    >>>…", "rrrwnrr", [2044, 1743, 2518, 4478, 985, 1596, 2182], ["", "", "", "EOFError: EOF when reading a line", "", "", ""], ["…'u'} return ''.join([char for char in text if char.lower() not in vowels]) ```", "…the input string. This ensures the solution is optimal even for longer strings.", "…This ensures the solution is optimal and handles all edge cases effectively.", "…which is straightforward and efficient for the given problem constraints."]],
    ["HumanEval/52", "Write the complete Python function `below_threshold` for this signature and docstring:\n\n\n\ndef below_threshold(l: list, t: int):\n    \"\"\"Return True if all numbers in the list l are below threshold t.\n    >>> below_threshold([1, 2, 4, 10], 100)\n    True\n    >>> below_threshold([1, 20, 4, 10], 5)\n    False\n    \"\"\"", "rrrrrrr", [877, 993, 1792, 1660, 866, 644, 1220], ["", "", "", "", "", "", ""], ["…and handles all edge cases, including lists with zero or one elements.", "…as soon as a False value is encountered, making it both concise and efficient.", "…20, 4, 10], 5) False \"\"\" return all(num < t for num in l) ```", "…that we efficiently determine the result with minimal computational overhead."]],
